{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-requiem/907480-wwycd-vampire-edition-night-of-the-living-dead","id":907480,"title":"WWYCD (Vampire Edition): Night of the Living Dead","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Vampire: The Requiem"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-06-04T23:30:36-07:00","id":907480,"title":"WWYCD (Vampire Edition): Night of the Living Dead","content":"The original <i>Night of the Living Dead </i>was on TV and it inspired this thought exercise (which I already posted in the Mage and Werewolf forums). It's a fun idea, and Vampire has its own share of twists on the idea, so let's get an idea for what your characters would do!<br /> <br /> Let's pose a Chronicles of Darkness version of the <i>Night of the Living Dead </i>scenario. The dead have begun to rise in a small town or city. It starts small, maybe even a local rundown graveyard or a cadaver suddenly awakening in a hospital. Maybe a patient dying in the hospital of a mysterious and rather gruesome illness. Reports of violent crimes across the county. Even cannibalism. Some force sporadically disrupts communications. Maybe similar reports come in from across the region, or even further out. Maybe you can't see that far, or don't have the luxury. After all, during the day you're as much a corpse as the ones that walk around eating people.<br /> <br /> The undead rise within minutes of anyone's death. They are tireless, mindlessly hungry, brutally strong. Some are fast, some are slow. Only destroying the brain or burning the body stops them. They can't be reasoned with, though they seem to have some ability to detect the living and travel in groups. A bite or scratch can transmit an almost universally-fatal wasting illness, although magic can cure it in those still living. Thankfully, vampires are immune, but can they be carriers? Better be careful! The origin is unknown. Is this a terrible plague loosed by blood magic gone awry? Some death god risen from cthonian depths? The malevolence of the Strix and their bloody, boundless hunger laid bare? No one knows. The mortal realm is becoming a nightmare, where people unbound by law and driven by desperation commit heinous acts just to survive. Ghosts stir to wrath and madness, all the more notable when vampires are <i>also </i>undead that must prey upon the living.<br /> <br /> What would your character do? How does he or she survive? How do your unnatural abilities aid you? How can you hide your nature in such a desperate time, and if you can't, what does it mean? You can use some examples of common scenarios: finding a place to hole up, aiding (or preying upon) other survivors, fighting zombies, going on food runs. You can even add in zombie animals if you like (I certainly like to use 'em!). Obviously you have to protect humans, or at least keep a few in reserve, because you need blood. All that food, all the places to hide within society, all the temporal power vampires so enjoy, it's all quickly dwindling. Are you going to turn on your fellow Kindred first or wait for them to turn on you? Does the appearance of mindless cannibal undead call into stark contrast your own unlife and what you've done with it? What's the difference between a draugr and a zombie in the end? How are you, a thinking vampire, any better if you descend into selfish hunger, using up what little you can find?<br /> <br /> Zombies don't attack vampires, at least those without the blush of life active. Eventually, someone might notice this. You might even use it to your advantage. Do you try to explore the cause of the undead rising, or find somewhere safer, more populated? Or is simply surviving it enough? Could you even last long in a shrinking community of scared survivors?<br /> <br /> When there is no more room in Hell, the dead will walk the Earth. The thing is, the dead <i>already </i>walk the Earth. You are \u2014 or were \u2014 supreme among hunters, hidden lords of the night. Now day and night are fallen victim to something with no Humanity, no pain, a tide of hungry undead that reflect the worst of what vampires can become. Are you going to rise above them and remain the Kindred ... or will you distinguish yourselves from the other cannibal undead only by the predatory cunning of your mind?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Freelancer </b>\u2022 Available for work!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/109-claire-redfield","name":"Claire Redfield","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar109_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"672"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-05T05:23:03-07:00","id":907572,"title":"","content":"I'm a little surprised it took this long for you to propose this idea, Claire, what with your username and avatar! BTW, my avatar is a photo of me at the Midnight release party for Resident Evil 5. As for what my character would do, I'll have to give that some thought...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/personality.htm\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://www.nodiatis.com/pub/12.jpg\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a></div> &quot;A free society is one in which it is safe to be unpopular.&quot;<br /> <span style=\"color:DarkRed\"><span style=\"font-size:20px\"><span style=\"font-family:Comic Sans MS\">I find <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=3&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwin4NXQzLfXAhVGySYKHV3TDXYQFgg3MAI&amp;url=http%3A%2F%2Fwww.ign.com%2Farticles%2F2017%2F04%2F25%2Fmarvels-nick-spencer-on-captain-americas-betrayal-and-handling-fan-reactions&amp;usg=AOvVaw2EcsX7n5ebntygb0TizyGl\" target=\"_blank\">Nick Spencer</a> and <a href=\"https://www.google.com/url?sa=t&amp;rct=j&amp;q=&amp;esrc=s&amp;source=web&amp;cd=4&amp;cad=rja&amp;uact=8&amp;ved=0ahUKEwiK7d7szLfXAhXCWSYKHTpKBbcQFgg4MAM&amp;url=https%3A%2F%2Fen.wikipedia.org%2Fwiki%2FRichard_B._Spencer&amp;usg=AOvVaw1tuP6phfINia-bh_jWsDT_\" target=\"_blank\">Richard Spencer</a> to be equally repulsive.</span></span></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6138-mangle77","name":"Mangle77","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6138_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"605"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-06T21:56:49-07:00","id":908885,"title":"","content":"First thing I (in character) would do would be to find a community of survivors. Next, identify someone influential in the group and ghoul them, with a full blood bond. Once that is done, it's time for the Masquerade to fall away. Using my ghoul as someone who will vouch for and defend me, I'd demonstrate what I was and my power to the group. Preferably, using some Majesty and Dominate for good measure. <br /> <br /> Once I was relatively sure of my safety, I'd make them a deal. Protect me during the day and let me feed a little bit from everyone healthy enough to withstand it. In exchange, I'll use my strength and relative immunity to the zombies to protect the community at night. I'd help them build barricades, clear out zombies, or whatever. One thing I wouldn't do is try to become the leader of the group. There would already be plenty of resentment at my presence and a power struggle would only make it worse.<br /> <br /> \u200bDepending on the size of the outbreak, there's several options from there. If it's small, try to find the source and end it. Once that's done, get out of Dodge. Sure, a bunch of crazy people might say a vampire helped them, but they also said they were attacked by zombies. Obviously, some sort of mass hysteria. If it's the end of the world, I'd try to save enough people to build an elite cadre of ghouls. For personal protection and also because they would (hopefully) be immune to the zombie plague if bitten/scratched. After I had my ghoul army, it's time to find an island and build a little kingdom, free from zombies and other Kindred. Although, if it was the end of the world, I might just catch a sunrise, because what's life without people?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1257-kerensky","name":"Kerensky","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1257_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"72"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-06-07T06:34:15-07:00","id":909107,"title":"","content":"Wonder if mental disciplines would work on zombies. Being able to dominate a zombie to get out of the way would make your stock go way up with humans (althought they could also start thinking you've been controlling them all along and bust out the pitchforks), and what you get from using telepathy on a zombie ? All those disciplines might get seriously twisted results and that could cause some fun.<br /> <br /> But yeah, this is probably a situation that (if it's getting desperate with no government support to expect soon) would justify breaking the masquerade. Another solution would be, for a mekhet or nosferatu, to keep on the edge of human groups. Making sure nothing happens to them by eliminating zombies that try to attack them. If vampires aren't targetted, then, the danger of sleeping during the day isn't that great. All you need is to find a hole in the ground that isn't going to crumble easily and away from places humans survivors would try to loot (don't sleep in a box of canned food in a supermarket).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7104-s-brechen","name":"S. Brechen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"171"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}